      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "CONSIGNMENT (4) broke his maiden two back when settling handy before tackling the G2 Sires'. Only fair there, but he'll be better for the experience and his trial coming into this was great. Resumes a gelding now and he can resume with a win. QUOKKA ROCKA (1) is the main danger, with his close fifth in Open company at this track before the break supported by a sound 1200m record and two trials. Looks ready to fire first-up with Li's claim a bonus. I'M A SOULMAN (7) was beaten as an odds-on favourite at York where he led them up and compounded late. He'll be fitter for that run and while this is tougher, the market last start suggests he's up to this. Don't discount him. LEVATI DIMEZZO (6) has placed in three of four starts and had excuses when second at Ascot on resumption. Can build on that effort. EXCELINDEED (5) was solid on resumption and can improve on that effort out to 1200m.",
